NNAAMMEE
     ddeevvffss..ccoonnff — boot-time devfs configuration information

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddeevvffss..ccoonnff file provides an easy way to set ownership and permis‐
     sions, or create links for devices available at boot.

     It does not work for devices plugged in and out after the system is up
     and running, e.g. USB devices.  See devfs.rules(5) for setting ownership
     and permissions for all device nodes, and devd.conf(5) for actions to be
     taken when devices are attached or detached.

     Lines starting with a hash sign (‘#’) and empty lines are ignored.  The
     lines that specify ddeevvffss..ccoonnff rules consist of three parameters separated
     by whitespace:

     _a_c_t_i_o_n  The action to take for the device.  The action names are only
             significant to the first unique character.

     _d_e_v_n_a_m_e
             The name of the device created by devfs(5).

     _a_r_g     The argument of the _a_c_t_i_o_n.

     The actions currently supported are:

     lliinnkk    This action creates a symbolic link named _a_r_g that points to
             _d_e_v_n_a_m_e, the name of the device created by devfs(5).

     oowwnn     This action changes the ownership of _d_e_v_n_a_m_e.  The _a_r_g parameter
             must be in the form of an _o_w_n_e_r:_g_r_o_u_p pair, in the same format
             used by chown(8).

     ppeerrmm    This action changes the permissions of _d_e_v_n_a_m_e.  The _a_r_g parame‐
             ter must be a _m_o_d_e as explained in chmod(1).

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/devfs.conf
     /usr/share/examples/etc/devfs.conf

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     To create a _/_d_e_v_/_c_d_r_o_m link that points to the first CD-ROM, the follow‐
     ing may be added to ddeevvffss..ccoonnff:

           link    cd0     cdrom

     To set the owner of a device, the oowwnn action may be specified:

           own     cd0     root:cdrom

     To set the permissions of a device, a ppeerrmm action should be used:

           perm    cd0     0660

